    "The active e71 inverse computes FP32 softmax, cumulative sum, searchsorted and a clamped bin index, then linear bar interpolation; it does not force terminal CDF=1 or clamp the interpolation fraction.",
    "The frozen SDK BarDistribution.icdf uses the same structure; FullSupportBarDistribution.sample calls inherited icdf. Half-normal formulas used by the class density do not imply half-normal sampling here.",
    "FP32 component uniforms are preassigned once per stage by row and retained across raw-mass head retries; accepted logits subsets and their original row uniforms enter the inverse.",
    "The raw canonical mass envelope is checked in FP64 before sampling, while the final logit softmax and inverse cumulative sum occur separately in FP32. A mass envelope does not prove a particular final cumulative endpoint or interpolation fraction.",
    "Canonical criterion borders are standard model borders scaled by training target standard deviation and mean; production validates finite FP32 borders, not a strict inverse-noise representability range.",
    "Strict noise decode uses log-tail formulas and a final open-interval test. A finite latent is therefore not a guarantee of representable interior physical output."
